CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member through the base path: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ nested list, constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
double delete: FAILURE$
dynamic object.*: FAILURE$
--
N5008 [dcl.init.aggr]/4-5, [dcl.init.list]/3.7: in `B b{{}, {owner(7), 3,
{4, 5}}, {1, 2}}' with `struct B : E { A a; C c; }' the member a, an
aggregate with a non-POD member, is aggregate-initialized from its list,
and c is initialized by C(int, int).  The aggregate-with-base path in
cpp_constructor assigned the braced list to the member, leaving an
initializer_list value that stopped symex with an invariant violation
(bin53).  An aggregate member is now aggregate-initialized member-wise
(aggregate_member_initialization) and other classes are list-initialized
by a constructor.  g++ 13 (with -fsanitize=address) and clang++ 18 accept
this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
